---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import SqlFormatter from '../../components/SqlFormatter.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="SQL Formatter" description="Format a messy or single-line SQL query into readable, keyword-aligned SQL.">
  <SqlFormatter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why format SQL</h2>
  <p>A single-line query pulled from a log file or ORM debug output is hard to scan for correctness. This tool breaks major clauses (SELECT, FROM, WHERE, JOIN, GROUP BY, ORDER BY) onto their own lines so you can review joins, filters, and ordering at a glance.</p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Breaks major SQL keywords onto new lines automatically</li>
    <li>Works with any SQL dialect's core keywords (SELECT, JOIN, WHERE, etc.)</li>
    <li>Instant, client-side formatting — nothing is sent to a server</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your SQL query into the input box, single-line or already partially formatted.</li>
    <li>The formatted version appears instantly below.</li>
    <li>Copy the result into your editor or query tool.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>Input: <code>select id, name from users where status = 'active' order by id limit 10</code></p>
  <p>Output:</p>
  <pre><code>SELECT id, name
FROM users
WHERE status = 'active'
ORDER BY id
LIMIT 10</code></pre>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming this validates your SQL.</strong> This tool only reformats spacing and line breaks — it doesn't check whether the query is syntactically valid or will run correctly.</li>
    <li><strong>Pasting queries with sensitive data</strong> (real customer records in WHERE clauses) into any online tool, even client-side ones — good habit is to use placeholder values when sharing/debugging.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cleaning up a minified query copied from application logs</li>
    <li>Making a long JOIN-heavy query readable before a code review</li>
    <li>Quickly reformatting a query generated by an ORM for debugging</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this validate my SQL syntax?</strong> No — it only reformats layout. Use a database client or linter to check validity.</p>
  <p><strong>Does it support all SQL dialects?</strong> It formats common keywords shared across PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server, and SQLite — dialect-specific syntax extensions aren't specially handled.</p>
</ToolLayout>
